*> PLB-C043 pointer-not-reset: STRING and UNSTRING start at their
*> POINTER and leave it past what they handled.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. POINTERS.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-REPLY            PIC X(80).
01  WS-REPLY-LENGTH     PIC 9(3) VALUE 1.
01  WS-PTR              PIC 9(3).
01  WS-FIELDS.
    05  WS-FIRST        PIC X(10).
    05  WS-SECOND       PIC X(10).
01  WS-INPUT            PIC X(40) VALUE "ONE,TWO".
01  WS-MESSAGES         PIC 9 VALUE 0.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-LINE.
    PERFORM BUILD-REPLY UNTIL WS-MESSAGES = 3
    PERFORM SPLIT-INPUT
    STOP RUN.
BUILD-REPLY.
    ADD 1 TO WS-MESSAGES
    STRING "REPLY " WS-MESSAGES DELIMITED BY SIZE
        INTO WS-REPLY WITH POINTER WS-REPLY-LENGTH
    END-STRING
    DISPLAY WS-REPLY(1:WS-REPLY-LENGTH).
SPLIT-INPUT.
    MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR
    UNSTRING WS-INPUT DELIMITED BY ","
        INTO WS-FIRST WS-SECOND WITH POINTER WS-PTR
    END-UNSTRING
    DISPLAY WS-FIELDS.
